// Secrets.example.xcconfig — template. Copy to Secrets.xcconfig (gitignored,
// see native-v2/.gitignore) and fill in real values. xcodegen wires
// Secrets.xcconfig into every build configuration via project.yml's
// top-level `configFiles:` block, and RouteMapView.swift reads the value
// back out of Info.plist (see Faff/Faff/Config/CartoConfig.swift) — the same
// two-step "build setting → Info.plist → Bundle.main lookup" idiom iOS apps
// use for any key that can't be a literal in source but also isn't sensitive
// enough to need Keychain / a server round-trip.
//
// xcodegen requires this file to EXIST at `xcodegen generate` time (it's
// referenced by path in the generated .pbxproj). If you don't have a key
// yet, keep this example file's blank value — the build still succeeds,
// RouteMapView just gets a 401 from CARTO instead of tiles.

// CARTO style key for the vector-tile "Dark Matter" MapLibre GL style
// (basemaps.cartocdn.com/gl/dark-matter-gl-style). Get one from CARTO's
// dashboard (Developers → API Keys). Same key as web's
// NEXT_PUBLIC_CARTO_API_KEY (web-v2/.env.example) — one CARTO account, one
// key, two surfaces.
CARTO_API_KEY =
